EX-J13 — Adaptive Gaborish kernel strength A/B (2026-05-18)
================================================================

Encoder:        jxl-encoder (in-tree, sibling workspace jxl-encoder--adaptive-gaborish)
Date:           2026-05-18 (UTC)
Parent commit:  zoqsvrww 45445443 feat(jpeg-transcode): EX-J17a (#49)
Reproduce:      cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --example adaptive_gaborish_ab
Image set:      3 CID22-512 validation + 2 CLIC2025-1024 photos (mixed smooth/textured)
Config:         LossyConfig::new(1.0).with_effort(7); A = with_adaptive_gaborish(false),
                B = with_adaptive_gaborish(true). Everything else default.
Mapping:        Per-tile (16x16) Y-channel mean |Laplacian| → mul ∈ [0.8, 1.0].
                contrast == 0           → mul = 0.8 (gentle, smooth tiles)
                contrast >= 0.05        → mul = 1.0 (libjxl baseline, edges)
Bytes-only.     Quality (butteraugli / SSIM2) not in this TSV — A and B both decode
                identically per the wire spec (decoder applies the same fixed
                3x3 inverse blur), so the bytes delta IS the RD delta at the
                same achieved quality.

Aggregate:      -1.74% bytes on 5 photos at d=1.0 e7 (467,394 -> 459,266 B).
Per-image:      -0.98% to -3.03%, all five smaller than baseline.

Hash-locks:     36/36 unchanged at default-off (test hash_lock_features).
